WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You lost a very closely
contested election,

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:07.340
an election in which there were,
you know, limited access to

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
polling places,
closed polling places,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.078 line:92%
polling places closing early.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems as though,
and, you know,

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not trying to
be unfair to Republicans,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.153
but it seems as though Democrats
want more people to vote

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Republicans
want the opposite.

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:25.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, Mitch McConnell told us
that he thought more people

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
being able to vote
was a power grab

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
because more people
who want power don't have it.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:34.167
And if we grab it from them,
they're not getting it back.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.102
-So, you have this organization
now, Fair Fight.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel optimistic that
we're going to move to a place

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.777 size:84% position:42%
where more people are,
you know, enfranchised?

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, so, I think we have to
think about it this way.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
Republicans have talked about
voter fraud,

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.550 size:88% position:44% line:92%
which is largely a myth.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they've talked about it
for so long, with such energy,

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.889 line:92%
that we take it as a truth.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those of us of good heart
and good conscience

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:01.127
and true democratic belief,
and I mean small "D" democratic,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:04.197
we know voter suppression is
real but we never talk about it.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.398 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We take it for granted.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
My belief is that
by calling it out

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
and by using
my non-concession speech

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:13.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my since actions
to demonstrate

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.307 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that we can fight back,

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.342 size:81% position:41%
that we can actually
reclaim our democracy.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.746
We've been practicing democracy
for a really long time.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
America gets it right
most of the time,

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when we stumble,
it is really bad.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:26.653
And my belief is that we've got
enough of us of good conscience

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
who will fight
to make it better.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just have to have someone
willing to talk about it

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:33.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
so we know that
we have a rallying cry

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:33.993 line:92%
and we have an opportunity.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got really close.
-You got really close.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.230 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.167 size:81% position:41%
You got really close
and it was a historic,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.635 line:92%
even with all the suppression,

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:46.706
it was a historic turnout
for a midterm election.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you did not --
when last you were here,

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.645
you were talking about you were
not out to flip Trump voters.

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.815
You were out to encourage people
who never voted before to vote.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.918
Do you feel like that should be,
as we go into 2020,

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.321
do you think that -- do you feel
good about that message?

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:04.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely. Look, my numbers
when I saw you in June,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:08.561
we wanted to hit -- we wanted
1.5 million people to vote.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got 1.9 million.
So we really did good.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:15.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:16.503 line:92%
-But what undergirded that is

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we tripled
the number of Latinos.

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.340 size:88% position:44%
We tripled the number of
Asian Pacific Islanders.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.210
We increased youth participation
rates by 139%.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
1.2 million African-Americans
voted for me.

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:31.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
1.1 million Democrats
voted in 2014.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
We know that if you talk to
communities

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.621 line:92%
that are normally ignored

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.257 size:75% position:38%
and if you fight for
their right to vote,

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:37.957 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you can win elections.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just can't have someone
acting as the referee,

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.695
the umpire, and the scorekeeper
also as your opponent.

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:46.900
-Yes, because your opponent was
the Secretary of State who was,

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.768 line:92%
of course, in charge of voting.

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:52.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
A little flaw in my process.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.205 --> 00:02:54.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everything else worked like
we thought.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.375 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Absolutely.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I hope
your process will continue.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course,
one of the things you did

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:02.215
that I hope the people
in your state will never forget,

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
you brought Oprah --
-I did.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And Oprah went
and canvassed voters.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:06.686 line:92%
And I'd like to finish --

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:09.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oprah Winfrey actually went
and knocked on doors.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:09.856 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And for people
who are wondering,

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
how would you react
if that happened to you?

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:17.931 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Here's a clip.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.699 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.234 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.268 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, my God!

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:24.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, Denise.
-Hi, Oprah.

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think -- I mean,
I hope you got her vote.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, God, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no, because they'll
accuse me of voter fraud.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
She lives in Illinois.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But she really helped --
Oh, you mean the young woman.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yes. Yes.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, got it.
Oprah would never.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because she is not registered
in Georgia.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-Thank you.

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
There we are.
Because fair is fair, right?

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:43.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
Fair is fair.
-In fact, we won a fair fight.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:45.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. There you go.
-Dot com.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is always such a pleasure
to see you.

